    <h1 class="rv in" style="font-size:clamp(2.2rem,5vw,4rem);max-width:20ch">Can You Rent a Boat Without a Skipper in Madeira?</h1>
    <div class="artmeta rv in d1"><span>21 November 2026</span><span>5 min read</span><span>Funchal · Madeira</span></div>
  </div>
</header>

<section class="pad">
  <div class="wrap">
    <article class="article rv">
      <p class="lede">Only if you hold a valid boat licence. Under Portugal&#x27;s recreational boating law, a boat may only sail under the command of someone with an appropriate navigator&#x27;s licence, and licences issued in other EU countries are recognised automatically. Without one, a boat with a skipper is the legal way onto Madeira&#x27;s coast.</p>

      <h2>What does Portuguese law actually say?</h2><p>The rule is short. Decree-Law 93/2018, Portugal's legal framework for recreational boating, says recreational boats may only sail under the command of people who hold an appropriate <em>carta de navegador de recreio</em>, the Portuguese navigator's licence, or of registered professional seafarers.</p><p>Breaking it is not a small matter. For a private person, the fine for sailing without the right licence runs from 300 to 3,000 EUR. You can read the decree itself in the <a href="https://diariodarepublica.pt/dr/detalhe/decreto-lei/93-2018-116950304" rel="noopener">Diário da República, Portugal's official gazette</a>.</p><p>Renting is a separate layer on top. The same decree says commercial use of recreational boats is governed by its own legislation, so a rental company adds its own conditions: which licences it accepts, a deposit, an area you must stay inside, or the weather it will not let you go out in.</p><h2>Which licence lets you drive which boat?</h2><p>Portugal grades its licences by boat size, engine power and how far from the coast you may go. The national maritime administration, DGRM, describes the categories like this:</p><table><thead><tr><th>Licence</th><th>Main limits</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Marinheiro Júnior</td><td>Boats up to 6 m and 4.5 kW, by day, within 1 mile of the low water line and 3 miles of a shelter port</td></tr><tr><td>Marinheiro</td><td>By day, within 3 miles of the coast and 10 miles of a shelter port. From 16 to 18, boats up to 6 m and 22.5 kW. Over 18, boats up to 12 m</td></tr><tr><td>Patrão Local</td><td>Within 6 miles of the coast and 25 miles of a shelter port</td></tr><tr><td>Patrão de Costa</td><td>Up to 40 miles from the coast</td></tr><tr><td>Patrão de Alto Mar</td><td>No area limit</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Look at the smallest licence. 4.5 kW is about 6 horsepower, the size of a small outboard on a dinghy, and the area stops one mile from shore. Nothing in that category takes you far along the south coast.</p><h2>Does a licence from home count?</h2><p>If it comes from another EU country, yes. The law recognises EU licences automatically, without a Portuguese one being issued. Licences from outside the EU are different: DGRM may recognise them when they were issued under requirements similar to Portugal's, and holders can in some cases apply for a Portuguese licence without an exam.</p><p>In practice, the company renting you the boat decides what it accepts, and it will ask to see your licence before it hands over the keys. Ask before you book, not at the marina.</p><h2>What about kayaks and paddle boards?</h2><p>They sit outside the boating law. The decree leaves out boards, with or without a sail, and canoes, kayaks and other beach craft without motor or sail that stay within 300 metres of the shore. You can paddle a board without any licence, and on our <a href="/hidden-coves-half-day">Day Trip with its swim stop at Fajã dos Padres</a> the paddle boards come with the boat.</p><h2>Why do most boat trips in Madeira come with a skipper?</h2><p>Because this is an open Atlantic coast, not a lake or a closed bay. West of Funchal towards Ribeira Brava the shore is mostly cliff, with few places to come in if the sea changes.</p><ul><li><strong>Swell travels.</strong> A storm far out in the Atlantic can send swell to a coast in full sunshine. It looks harmless from a hotel balcony and feels very different under a cliff.</li><li><strong>Cliffs shed stones.</strong> Cabo Girão rises about 580 metres. Keeping your distance from the foot of a cliff is basic, and it is easy to drift close while everyone is looking up.</li><li><strong>Swim stops are chosen, not found.</strong> Which side of Fajã dos Padres is calm today, whether jumping in is safe, where to hold the boat while people swim: that is local knowledge, not something a chart shows.</li><li><strong>The marina.</strong> Bringing a boat into Marina do Funchal with others moving around you takes practice.</li></ul><h2>What does a skippered trip cover in a few hours?</h2><p>More than most people expect, because nobody loses time learning the boat. In 2h30 the Day Trip, at 10:00 or 14:00, takes in Câmara de Lobos, the foot of Cabo Girão, a swim and a paddle at Fajã dos Padres and another swim at Ribeira Brava, and the 3h version gets as far as Ponta do Sol. The evening Sunset Trip covers less coast and is about the light more than the miles.</p><h2>What does the skipper add to the day?</h2><p>Mostly, the freedom to stop thinking about the boat. Chifbay's two skippers are local professionals, and with one of them at the helm:</p><ul><li>nobody in your group has to stay sober to drive, so the local wine, poncha and beer on board are for everyone;</li><li>everyone can swim, jump in and paddle at the same time, because someone stays with the boat;</li><li>you are in the real camera photos, the 360° video and, when the weather allows, the drone footage, because nobody has to steer;</li><li>the call on whether the sea is safe is made by a professional who knows this coast. A day judged unsafe means a new date or your money back, never a gamble.</li></ul><p>Chifbay holds a maritime tourism licence, RNAAT n.º 305/2026. To check any company before you book, licensed or not, read our guide on <a href="/posts/how-to-check-a-boat-tour-operator-in-madeira-is-licensed">how to check a boat operator's licence in Madeira</a>.</p><h2>When does a boat without a skipper make sense?</h2><p>It depends on you. If you hold a proper licence, have handled a motorboat at sea before and want a quiet day at your own pace, renting without a skipper is a fair choice. Ask the company about insurance, the deposit, the area you may use and what happens if the forecast turns.</p><p>If you have never driven a boat on open water, Madeira is not the place to learn on holiday. Book a <a href="/boat-rental-with-skipper-funchal">boat with a skipper from Funchal</a> or a <a href="/private-boat-tour-madeira">private boat tour in Madeira</a>, and spend the day in the water instead of at the wheel. Before any trip, our guide to <a href="/posts/madeira-sea-conditions-boat-trip-guide">sea conditions in Madeira</a> explains what the forecast numbers mean.</p><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><h3>Is a licence needed for a paddle board or a kayak?</h3><p>No. The recreational boating law does not cover paddle boards, nor canoes and kayaks without motor or sail that stay within 300 metres of the shore.</p><h3>Is an EU boat licence valid in Madeira?</h3><p>Yes. Licences issued in other EU countries are recognised automatically in Portugal. A rental company can still set its own conditions.</p><h3>What is the fine for driving a boat without a licence in Portugal?</h3><p>Under Decree-Law 93/2018, the fine for a private person runs from 300 to 3,000 EUR.</p><h3>Who decides if the sea is safe on a skippered trip?</h3><p>The skipper. When they judge it unsafe, nobody goes out, and you rebook or get a full refund.</p>

      <blockquote>The licence lets you drive. The coast decides whether you should.</blockquote>
    </article>
    <p class="pref-src" data-pref-source><span>Enjoying our Madeira guides?</span> <a href="https://www.google.com/preferences/source?q=chifbay.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" aria-hidden="true"><path fill="#4285F4" d="M23.5 12.3c0-.8-.1-1.6-.2-2.3H12v4.5h6.5a5.6 5.6 0 0 1-2.4 3.6v3h3.9c2.2-2.1 3.5-5.1 3.5-8.8z"/><path fill="#34A853" d="M12 24c3.2 0 6-1.1 7.9-2.9l-3.9-3c-1.1.7-2.4 1.2-4 1.2-3.1 0-5.7-2.1-6.6-4.9h-4v3.1A12 12 0 0 0 12 24z"/><path fill="#FBBC05" d="M5.4 14.4a7.2 7.2 0 0 1 0-4.7V6.6h-4a12 12 0 0 0 0 10.8l4-3z"/><path fill="#EA4335" d="M12 4.8c1.7 0 3.3.6 4.6 1.8l3.4-3.4A12 12 0 0 0 1.4 6.6l4 3.1C6.3 6.9 8.9 4.8 12 4.8z"/></svg>Add Chifbay as a preferred source on Google</a></p>

